stateDiagram-v2
    accTitle: A Claude task's statuses
    accDescr: A task Alfred hands to a Claude worker on Kevin's laptop is queued, claimed and run, and finishes done, failed, needs_confirmation or cancelled. A yes to "Ship it?" is a new child task, so needs_confirmation is terminal.
    %% Source: server/claude_session/models.py (status choices, TERMINAL), views.py
    %% (TaskListCreateView, TaskAssignView, ClaimView, TaskCancelView, FinishView), state.py.
    state "needs machine" as needs_machine
    state "cancel requested" as cancel_requested
    state "needs confirmation" as needs_confirmation
    [*] --> queued: created, one machine known
    [*] --> needs_machine: created, several machines online
    needs_machine --> queued: assigned a machine
    queued --> running: claimed by the worker
    queued --> cancelled: cancelled
    needs_machine --> cancelled: cancelled
    running --> cancel_requested: cancel asked
    running --> done: finished
    running --> failed: finished, or 30 min cap
    running --> needs_confirmation: asks "Ship it?"
    cancel_requested --> cancelled: worker stopped it
    cancel_requested --> done
    cancel_requested --> failed
    done --> [*]
    failed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]
    needs_confirmation --> [*]: a yes is a new task (confirms, parent)
